    "original_text": "Attributed scoped prerequisite/interface restatement:\nE is a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space, including zero dimension. kappa>=1, f:E->R is globally C2 and its actual nested second derivative satisfies (2kappa)^-1||v||²<=D²f(z)[v,v]<=||v||² for every z,v. Producing the actual source f=V_eta remains open.\nJ>=2,h>0; t_j=h(1-cos(j*pi/(J-1)))/2, cardinal ell_j, and omega_ij=integral_0^t_i(t_i-s)ell_j(s)ds, b_j=integral_0^h ell_j(s)ds,c_j=integral_0^h(h-s)ell_j(s)ds are the actual coefficients. Lambda=sup_[0,h] sum_j |ell_j| and actual hLambda<=1/(65536kappa).\na=exp(-h/2),sigma=sqrt(1-exp(-h)); P0=a p+sigma zeta0, Y0_j=x+t_jP0, Y1_i=Y0_i-sum_j omega_ij gradient f(Y0_j), Phi=(x+hP0-sum_j c_j gradient f(Y1_j),a(P0-sum_j b_j gradient f(Y1_j))+sigma zeta1). Gamma=standard Gaussian E product standard Gaussian E, with independent refresh vectors.\nBoth input laws mu,nu are arbitrary probability laws on phase space; their source quadratic transport may be infinite. Q_kappa(x,p)=((2kappa)^-1+1/2)||x||²+inner(x,p)+||p||², c_kappa(z,zprime)=ofReal Q_kappa(z-zprime), and W_M²=T_c_kappa. Source Q is retained, not the ordinary product max norm.\nConstruct a Markov K whose law at every z is Gamma.map(zeta -> Phi(z,zeta)). For all probability mu,nu, K composed with each input equals the actual pushforward Phi#(input×Gamma), and W_M²(Kmu,Knu)<=(1-h/(65536kappa))² W_M²(mu,nu). This is the actual deterministic exact-gradient Gaussian numerical kernel, not an arbitrary supplied contracting kernel and not an invariant-target theorem.\nActual Gaussian exact-gradient numerical K at the explicit normalized global C2 curvature interface. Actual f=V_eta smoothing/C2/curvature remains separate. No target invariance/stationarity, numerical target bias, stochastic Khat/Kbar, local errors/history/expected query cost, Wp/proxy-warmness/initialization, PBPS or either complete main/composition result. TV proximity does not transfer unbounded cost.",
    "text_sha256": "df23d392880fc9288a660b5790fb8d41ff314571b84c7aaec93e10646273f43c"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.ActualKernelTransport.source_kernel_transport_contraction",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/SmoothedPicardHMC/ActualKernelTransport.lean",
    "statement": "{f : E → ℝ} {κ h : ℝ} {J : ℕ}\n    (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 2 f)\n    (hH : ∀ z v, (1 / (2 * κ)) * ‖v‖ ^ 2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ f) z v) v ∧\n      (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ f) z v) v ≤ ‖v‖ ^ 2)\n    (hJ : 2 ≤ J) (hh : 0 < h) :\n    let t := fun i : Fin J => h/2*(1-Real.cos ((i : ℝ)/(J-1 : ℝ)*Real.pi))\n    let ell := fun j : Fin J => Lagrange.basis Finset.univ t j\n    let Λ := sSup ((fun s : ℝ => ∑ j : Fin J, |(ell j).eval s|) '' Icc 0 h)\n    let ω := fun i j : Fin J => ∫ s in 0..t i, (t i-s)*(ell j).eval s\n    let b := fun j : Fin J => ∫ s in 0..h, (ell j).eval s\n    let c := fun j : Fin J => ∫ s in 0..h, (h-s)*(ell j).eval s\n    h * Λ ≤ 1/(65536*κ) →\n    let a := Real.exp (-h / 2)\n    let sigma := Real.sqrt (1 - Real.exp (-h))\n    let P0 := fun (z ζ : E × E) => a • z.2 + sigma • ζ.1\n    let Y0 := fun (z ζ : E × E) j => z.1 + t j • P0 z ζ\n    let Y1 := fun (z ζ : E × E) i => Y0 z ζ i - ∑ j, ω i j • gradient f (Y0 z ζ j)\n    let Φ := fun w : (E × E) × (E × E) =>\n      (w.1.1 + h • P0 w.1 w.2 - ∑ j, c j • gradient f (Y1 w.1 w.2 j),\n        a • (P0 w.1 w.2 - ∑ j, b j • gradient f (Y1 w.1 w.2 j)) + sigma • w.2.2)\n    let Γ := (stdGaussian E).prod (stdGaussian E)\n    ∃ K : Kernel (E × E) (E × E), IsMarkovKernel K ∧\n      (∀ z, K z = Γ.map (fun ζ => Φ (z,ζ))) ∧\n      ∀ (μ ν : Measure (E × E)), IsProbabilityMeasure μ → IsProbabilityMeasure ν →\n        K ∘ₘ μ = (μ.prod Γ).map Φ ∧ K ∘ₘ ν = (ν.prod Γ).map Φ ∧\n        phaseWassersteinSq κ (K ∘ₘ μ) (K ∘ₘ ν) ≤\n          ENNReal.ofReal ((1-h/(65536*κ))^2) * phaseWassersteinSq κ μ ν",
    "statement_sha256": "30ccf5ee9a16f379239ec6ea6844e7f1b034bac1dcd051fe6a60657e97055576",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "E is a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable space. ContDiff R 2 f means globally C2; fderiv R (fderiv R f) is its actual second derivative, and gradient f is the Riesz representative of its derivative.",
      "Fin J indexes0 through J-1; Lagrange.basis gives cardinal polynomials at the displayed nodes, eval is polynomial evaluation, sSup is the real supremum. Interval integrals are ordinary Lebesgue Bochner integrals.",
      "stdGaussian E is the standard centered identity-covariance Gaussian measure. Gamma is the independent product of two such laws, used for the two refreshes of the displayed actual Phi. Kernel means a measurable probability-transition measure family; IsMarkovKernel means probability at every state. K composed with mu is measure/kernel composition.",
      "phaseQuadraticForm kappa (x,p)=((1/(2*kappa))+(1/2))*norm(x)^2+inner R x p+norm(p)^2; phaseCost kappa (z,zprime)=ENNReal.ofReal(phaseQuadraticForm kappa (z-zprime)). phaseWassersteinSq kappa mu nu is the raw infimum of the lintegral of that cost over all measures gamma with gamma.fst=mu and gamma.snd=nu. No optimizer or finite moment convention is imposed. Measure.prod is independent product and Measure.map is pushforward."
    ],
    "compiler_evidence": "Focused3717 actual nonconstant-Hessian full Gaussian numerical kernel/all probability-law test; standard3 only. Independent mathematics/source review pending."
  },
