        "Both input laws mu,nu are arbitrary probability laws on phase space; their source quadratic transport may be infinite. Q_kappa(x,p)=((2kappa)^-1+1/2)||x||²+inner(x,p)+||p||², c_kappa(z,zprime)=ofReal Q_kappa(z-zprime), and W_M²=T_c_kappa. Source Q is retained, not the ordinary product max norm."
      ],
      "statement": "Construct a Markov K whose law at every z is Gamma.map(zeta -> Phi(z,zeta)). For all probability mu,nu, K composed with each input equals the actual pushforward Phi#(input×Gamma), and W_M²(Kmu,Knu)<=(1-h/(65536kappa))² W_M²(mu,nu). This is the actual deterministic exact-gradient Gaussian numerical kernel, not an arbitrary supplied contracting kernel and not an invariant-target theorem.",
      "formula": "K(z)=\\Phi_z{}_{\\#}\\Gamma,\\quad K\\mu=\\Phi_\\#(\\mu\\otimes\\Gamma),\\quad W_{2,M_\\kappa}^2(K\\mu,K\\nu)\\le\\left(1-\\frac{h}{65536\\kappa}\\right)^2W_{2,M_\\kappa}^2(\\mu,\\nu).",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Recover actual joint measurability",
          "text": "The genuine source quadrature constructor gives Lambda>=1. The actual step condition gives h<=1 and h²Lambda<=1. Reuse FirstOrderDifference for exactly the same coefficients/potential/Phi; its jointly measurable actual numerical map is the needed random-map producer.",
          "formula": "\\Lambda_J\\ge1,\\quad h\\le1,\\quad h^2\\Lambda_J\\le1,\\quad\\Phi\\text{ jointly measurable}.",
          "lean": "hcoeff; hLambda; hs; hfirst.1; hΦ"
        },
        {
          "title": "Build the Markov kernel and prove both laws",
          "text": "Use (id times const Gamma).map Phi. Markovness follows from actual independent probability refreshes and measurable Phi. At each z, dirac×Gamma followed by map composition gives Gamma.map(Phi_z). For any probability input, the map-composition and constant-kernel product identities yield Kmu=Phi#(mu×Gamma). These identities justify the actual kernel semantics before applying a law-level inequality.",
          "formula": "K=(\\mathrm{id}\\times\\mathrm{const}\\,\\Gamma).\\mathrm{map}\\,\\Phi,\\qquad K\\mu=\\Phi_\\#(\\mu\\otimes\\Gamma).",
          "lean": "K; hK; Kernel.map_apply; Kernel.prod_apply; Measure.dirac_prod; hlaw; Measure.map_comp; Measure.compProd_eq_comp_prod; Measure.compProd_const"
        },
        {
          "title": "Square the actual source norm contraction",
          "text": "The existing ActualContraction theorem proves the source Q norm contraction for every input and common noise, using the actual numerical phase. Delta=1-h/(65536kappa) is strictly positive. The unchanged Q lower comparison gives nonnegative Q for all phase displacements. Square the genuine sqrt inequality and reuse the squared sqrt identity, then apply ofReal multiplication. This proves the measurable extended pointwise cost bound with A=ofReal(delta²); it is not a public supplied premise of this consumer.",
